chrony protocol acknowledgement

The libchronyctl component communicates with the chronyd daemon using the chrony Command And
Monitoring (CANDM) binary wire protocol.  The protocol was designed by Richard P. Curnow and
Miroslav Lichvar as part of the chrony project (https://chrony-project.org).

The wire-protocol structure definitions, command codes, reply codes, and field layouts in
libchronyctl/chrony_protocol.h and libchronyctl/chrony_address.h were independently written
to describe that published binary protocol.  No source code was copied from the chrony project.
(The presence of structurally similar protocol definitions, fields etc. is a necessary
consequence of implementing a compatible client for the same binary wire format.)
